  "query_preview": "../ Thursday to Monday / Aloft the steering levels of  \nthe atmosphere has a long wave trough finally being ejected from \nthe gulf late Thursday to Friday, followed by a sharper moderate-\nhigh amplitude ridge that reaches near to arctic shores. Ridge \nwill slide east of the panhandle by late Sunday, as the Large \nBering Sea low from the western Bering Sea weakens but shift to \nthe eastern portion of the Bering. With the ridge axis east of the\narea, noticed a pair of short waves, one Sunday evening pushing \nthrough the panhandle over the ridge top, and second one which may\nbe slightly stronger for the Monday time frame. \n\nSo what does this mean weather wise for Southeast... showers from\nthe midweek into Thursday, tapering off/ending as improvements \nFriday - early Saturday period due to the ridge moving through and\nclearing weather out. After the ridge slides by rain will start to\npush back in into the NE Gulf then Northern panhandle late \nSaturday to Sunday. Models beginning to come to agreement of \nfairly organized from to push through the eastern gulf Sunday to \nMonday. A secondary low that formed on the front towards the \nYakutat Pocket and the front trailing south then southwest, with \nlikely another trailing low on the front to run along and slowing \nit down to impact the southern panhandle most likely the hardest. \nWill watch how models adjust over the next few runs. \n\nIn short longer range is wet, dry break Friday-Saturday and then\nwet into next week. Temperature-wise at or just below normal\nvalues, with higher elevations of the Klondike and the higher\nCanadian Haines Highways to possible see snow or snow rain mix for\nthe weekend period.",
